"""Pinebook Pro control service, behind the Pinebook app.

Runs as root from the upstart job pinebook-control and serves the app at
http://pinebook.localhost:8086/ (localhost only):

GET  /api/status    CPU and GPU frequencies and load, temperatures, battery
                    and estimated power, memory, and which programs use the
                    GPU and the hardware video decoders.
GET  /api/settings  The saved settings and what the hardware allows.
POST /api/settings  Saves and applies the CPU/GPU limits right away, and
                    writes or removes the boot-time tuning (overclock,
                    undervolt).

Limits (governor, maximum frequency) are applied through cpufreq and devfreq
at every start of the service. Overclocking and undervolting change the OPP
tables in the device tree, so they take effect at the next boot: the service
writes pinebook-tune.scr (a U-Boot script of fdt commands) to the card's
EFI-SYSTEM partition, and the board's boot.scr runs it. Deleting that file
(from any computer: EFI-SYSTEM is FAT) brings back the stock tables.

POST requests need the X-Pinebook header (which a page from another origin
cannot send without a CORS preflight, and this server answers none) and a
matching Origin; every request needs a localhost Host header.
"""

